Let $K$ be a number field and $X$ be a left homogeneous space under a connected algebraic group $G/K$, satisfying $\Sha(K,G^{ab})$ finite. We assume that the $G$-action on $X$ has connected geometric stabilizers. Let $\B_{\infty}(X) \subset \mathrm{Br}_{1,ur}(X)$ be defined as:
	\begin{equation}
		\B_{\infty}(X) \ensuremath{\coloneqq} \mathrm{Ker} \left(\mathrm{Br}_{1}(X) \rightarrow \prod_{v \in M_K^{fin}}\mathrm{Br} (X_{K_v})/\mathrm{Br} K_v\right).
	\end{equation}
	We then have that $X(K)\neq \emptyset$ if and only if $X(\mathbb{A}_K)^{\B_{\infty}(X)}\neq \emptyset$.

Let $v \in M_K$, $x \in X(K_v)$ be a local point, and $B \in \mathbb{H}^2(K_v,C_X^d)$. Then one has that:
	\begin{equation}
	<x,\alpha(B)>=<\mathrm{ab}_{K_v}^0(x),B>,
	\end{equation}
	where:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item the first pairing is the local Brauer pairing;

		\item the second pairing is the one induced by 

		the local pairing (3.6).
	\end{itemize}
